# Pages

Rules for files under `app/pages/`. Follow global rules in `global.mdc`.

## Current starter

`app/pages/index.vue` is the home page. It uses the default layout and renders a `.page-wrapper`. There is no auth redirect and no feature routes.

```vue
<template>
  <main class="page-wrapper">
    <h1>Nuxt Template</h1>
    <p>Start building from this page.</p>
  </main>
</template>

<script setup lang="ts">
definePageMeta({
  layout: 'default',
})
</script>

<style scoped></style>
```

Replace this page when the product has a real home. Do not leave marketing or demo sections in the template.

## Routing

| File | Route | Role |
|------|-------|------|
| `index.vue` | `/` | Home |
| `feature.vue` | parent of `/feature/*` | Layout and middleware only |
| `feature/index.vue` | `/feature` | Section home |
| `feature/create/index.vue` | `/feature/create` | Create form |
| `feature/edit/[id].vue` | `/feature/edit/:id` | Edit by id |

- Use kebab-case folders (`voice-record-file/`).
- Use bracket params: `[id].vue`.
- Prefer `index.vue` for the default child route.

## Parent wrappers

A section with children gets a thin parent. The parent chooses the layout and middleware. Child files hold the UI.

```vue
<template>
  <NuxtLayout name="main-content">
    <NuxtPage />
  </NuxtLayout>
</template>

<script setup lang="ts">
definePageMeta({
  layout: 'default',
  middleware: ['user-only'],
})
</script>
```

Add `middleware` only after that middleware file exists.

## Leaf pages

Block order: template, `<script setup lang="ts">`, scoped style.

Script order:

1. Imports
2. `useRoute()` / `useRouter()` and page meta
3. Local state
4. Composables
5. Handlers
6. `onMounted` and watchers

- Fetch through a composable when one exists. Do not call services from the page in that case.
- List pages show loading, an empty state, and pagination when there is more than one page.
- Forms use `reactive()` for fields, validate before submit, and navigate back to the list on success.
- Read dynamic ids from `route.params`.
- Navigate with `useRouter().push()`.

## What does not belong in pages

- The app shell (use a layout).
- Large blocks copied across routes (extract a component).
- HTTP URLs and DTO mapping (use services).
- Global session state (use a store).
